      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Lumbar pain is common among cricket's fast bowlers, leading to premature retirement. The cause of a high incidence of back problems lies in the repetitive spinal movements necessary in the art of fast bowling. This combines repetitive lateral flexion, thoraco-dorsal rotation, spinal flexion and compression. The causes are basically too much bowling by young players with relatively immature pars interarticularis, poor physical fitness and a poor bowling action."},
